 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": "c-p1-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### What normalization is for",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 1,
    "blockIds": [
     "p1-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p1-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Redundancy is one fact stored in more than one row",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 1,
    "blockIds": [
     "p1-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p1-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Insert, update and delete anomalies all follow from it",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 1,
    "blockIds": [
     "p1-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p1-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- A table that repeats a fact can be made to contradict itself",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 1,
    "blockIds": [
     "p1-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p1-b4",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- The normal forms are a sequence of guarantees, each stricter",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 1,
    "blockIds": [
     "p1-b4"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p2-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### Functional dependency",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 2,
    "blockIds": [
     "p2-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p2-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- A → B: any two rows agreeing on A must agree on B",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 2,
    "blockIds": [
     "p2-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p2-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- A claim about every row the table will ever hold",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 2,
    "blockIds": [
     "p2-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p2-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Read it off the meaning of the data, never off a sample",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 2,
    "blockIds": [
     "p2-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p2-b4",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "X → A holds when any two rows equal on X are also equal on A",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 2,
    "blockIds": [
     "p2-b4"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p3-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### Keys, from dependencies",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 3,
    "blockIds": [
     "p3-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p3-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Superkey: an attribute set that determines all the others",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 3,
    "blockIds": [
     "p3-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p3-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Candidate key: a superkey with nothing left to remove",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 3,
    "blockIds": [
     "p3-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p3-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Prime attribute: one that belongs to some candidate key",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 3,
    "blockIds": [
     "p3-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p3-b4",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Every normal form below is stated in these three words",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 3,
    "blockIds": [
     "p3-b4"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p4-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### First normal form",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 4,
    "blockIds": [
     "p4-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p4-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Every attribute holds one indivisible value",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 4,
    "blockIds": [
     "p4-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p4-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- No repeating groups: no phone1, phone2, phone3",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 4,
    "blockIds": [
     "p4-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p4-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- No lists in a cell, however convenient they look",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 4,
    "blockIds": [
     "p4-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### Why a list in a cell hurts",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- It cannot be joined against, constrained, or usefully indexed",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Reading one entry means reading and parsing all of them",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Split the group into its own relation, keyed by the parent",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b4",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- The cost is one join; the gain is a database that can check it",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b4"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b5",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "Id Name Phones",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b5"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b6",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "17 Ada 555-0101, 555-0144",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b6"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b7",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "18 Ben 555-0172",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b7"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p5-b8",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "19 Cem 555-0118, 555-0190, 555-0135",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 5,
    "blockIds": [
     "p5-b8"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p6-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### Partial dependency",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 6,
    "blockIds": [
     "p6-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p6-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Only possible under a composite key",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 6,
    "blockIds": [
     "p6-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p6-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- A non-prime attribute depending on part of that key",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 6,
    "blockIds": [
     "p6-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p6-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- (order, product) → quantity, but product alone → product name",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 6,
    "blockIds": [
     "p6-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p7-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### Second normal form",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 7,
    "blockIds": [
     "p7-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p7-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- In 1NF, and no non-prime attribute depends on part of a key",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 7,
    "blockIds": [
     "p7-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p7-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Project the partial dependency out into its own relation",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 7,
    "blockIds": [
     "p7-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p7-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Automatic when the key is a single attribute — no part to depend on",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 7,
    "blockIds": [
     "p7-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p8-b0",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "### The update anomaly, worked",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 8,
    "blockIds": [
     "p8-b0"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p8-b1",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Product name repeated on every order line naming that product",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 8,
    "blockIds": [
     "p8-b1"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p8-b2",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Renaming it means finding every one of those lines",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 8,
    "blockIds": [
     "p8-b2"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p8-b3",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "- Miss one and two rows now disagree about the same product",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 8,
    "blockIds": [
     "p8-b3"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "id": "c-p8-b4",
   "origin": "extracted",
   "markdown": "Order Product Quantity Product name",
   "source": {
    "materialId": "m-norm",
    "page": 8,
    "blockIds": [
     "p8-b4"
    ]
   },
   "edited": false
  },
